# INFERNO alone, the 3 minutes survived with every life.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame inferno --headless --ms 180900 --input tools/play/inferno-alone-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame inferno --headless --ms 180900 --fix all --input tools/play/inferno-alone-win.input
#
# The keys are `tools/inferno_plan.py` (planned against the port): the hero
# stands at x 153, under no platform, and jumps (UP) 1.9 s before each
# hazard would reach him, so he lands on it from above: 32 stomps, +150
# each, 4800 points. He never walks (no scroll zone: H7 never matters),
# never runs into a hazard from the side (H5) and loses no life (H6), so
# the Original and the Corrigida play the same game. At 180000 the clock
# reports (5 lives, 500): the flat win, whatever the score. The Original
# reposts it every 100 ms (H2) and a second later spins on WM_DESTROY for
# good (BUGS.md H8: the port panics at 181000), hence --ms 180900; with
# `--fix all` INFERNO quits at 181000.
